'''Trading''' is a feature that allows players to trade items and {{Coins}} with each other.

== Overview ==
=== Initiating a Trade ===
To initiate a trade with another player, the player can either:
* use the {{Code|/trade <player>}} command;
* interact with the person they wish to trade with through {{Keypress|Shift}} + {{Keypress|Right Click}};
* or click on the {{Item|Emerald|link=}} in their profile menu, which will initiate a trade request.
The recipient will receive the following message in chat:
{{Dialogue|&a<username> has sent you a trade request. &bClick here &ato accept!}}
The maximum distance you can trade from is {{Green|9}} blocks.

=== Tradeable Items ===
Almost all items can be traded, alongside a given lump-sum of {{Coins}}. Some items that cannot be put up for auction on the [[Auction House]], such as [[Minions]] and certain items from {{NPCSprite|Anita}}, can be traded; other items cannot be auctioned or traded at all, such as [[Sacks]].

Items that are {{Soulbound}} cannot be traded at all, and items that are {{Co-op Soulbound}} cannot be traded with players outside of the player's [[Co-op]].

=== Trading Coins ===
A given lump-sum of {{Coins}} can be traded in the Trading menu. Players under [[SkyBlock Levels|{{Aqua|SkyBlock Level 50}}]] have a daily trading limit of  {{c|50m}} players above [[SkyBlock Levels|{{Aqua|SkyBlock Level 50}}]] have a limit of {{c|1b}}, and players above [[SkyBlock Levels|{{Aqua|SkyBlock Level 100}}]] have a limit of {{c|10b}}.

Different icons in the Trading menu show different amounts of {{Coins}}
* [[File:Coins.png|21px]] represents {{c|1-99999}};
* [[File:Coin Tier 2.png|21px]] represents {{c|100000-9999999}};
* [[File:Coins (Lapis).png|21px]] represents {{Gold|≥}}{{c|10m}}.

=== Restrictions ===
[[Ironman|{{Gray|♻ Ironman}}]], [[Stranded|{{Green|☀ Stranded}}]], and [[Bingo|{{DarkPurple|Ⓑ Bingo}}]] players are explicitly restricted from trading. Additionally, players using a nickname cannot trade with anyone other than players with the {{Rank|h}} rank.

